From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 12:59:25 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 8/8] His voice: the owner's recorded lines said as his
 thoughts and words come up

Fourteen recordings (trimmed, levelled to -18 LUFS, mono): each thought is said as it comes up and
stays until it is said; the invitation and the thoughts in the car are said as typed (the car's lines
keep pace with the recording) and the story waits for the last word. The voice bypasses the world's
muffling, the ambience ducks under it; nothing is said with the sound off; skip stops it. Captions
now say what the recordings say (the extra 'most' cut from line 3's recording).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_017Yfam9H7FbQFsBx6yJZ8yW
